  "finalText": "Positioning the loaf and checking the frames next.\nI built the 6 s piece on a warm cream background, but I haven't looked at a frame since the last nudge to the loaf's position.\n\n- **Lines:** the wobbly **stalk** draws on from 0.6 s and the **loaf** from 1.2 s, both with soft Sine In Out strokes in brown. They boil in 12 fps steps, jittering a couple of pixels and rotating about half a degree each frame, so they read as hand-animated.\n- **Blobs:** **blob1** (ochre), **blob2** (sage) and **blob3** (terracotta) fade in staggered and breathe slowly at slightly different rates.\n- **Name:** \"Crumb & Co\" in Georgia pops in letter by letter from 3 s with a soft spring. The tagline \"baked by hand, with love\" fades up at 4 s.\n\nI didn't run critique or fix anything beyond positioning. The earlier frames showed the name wrapping, so I widened its box. I also moved the stalk and loaf onto their blobs, and the last check had the layout balanced.\n\nI can make the boil rougher or calmer, slow the draw-on, or add a loop so it repeats cleanly."
